{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38348540",
      "title": "Lifting the State Up",
      "sourceHash": "36333a77eaaa71c75f823d854c84d179daa1fe7222fb3c7ac4bb31b537b24000",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.87,
          "en": "So now that we're gathering all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.87,
          "end": 6.96,
          "en": "that user input, we now need to find a way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.96,
          "end": 9.96,
          "en": "of deriving the results that should ultimately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.96,
          "end": 13.031,
          "en": "be output here in the Results Table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.031,
          "end": 17.4,
          "en": "So we need to get this user input in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 19.62,
          "en": "from this user input component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.62,
          "end": 21.832,
          "en": "to the Results Table component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.832,
          "end": 25.26,
          "en": "Though technically the Results Table component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.26,
          "end": 28.23,
          "en": "of course, won't care about the user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 31.95,
          "en": "but instead on the calculation results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.95,
          "end": 34.59,
          "en": "So we'll need to perform the calculation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 37.143,
          "en": "that's set up here in App.JS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.269,
          "end": 41.155,
          "en": "So in the end, put in other words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.155,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "we have some state in user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 48.222,
          "en": "The user input values, that's the state I mean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.222,
          "end": 51.513,
          "en": "which is received in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.462,
          "end": 57.462,
          "en": "but which in the end, in transformed form is needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 60.69,
          "en": "in the Results Table component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.69,
          "end": 65.1,
          "en": "And what do you do if you have a situation like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.1,
          "end": 68.19,
          "en": "Well, you lift state up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.19,
          "end": 70.14,
          "en": "That's what you learned in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.61,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "And actually here the app component is already configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 77.342,
          "en": "to perform this calculation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.342,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "and to receive this user input state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "So here, lifting the state up is quite straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 86.463,
          "en": "and you don't have to do a lot for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 90.15,
          "en": "One thing you need to do though is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 94.928,
          "en": "in user input in this component, you'll need to accept props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.928,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "because you'll need to accept a function as a prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 102.72,
          "en": "a function, which you can call inside of user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.72,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "but which will be defined in App.JS in the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "And it's this calculate handler function, I mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 112.25999999999999,
          "en": "This should be triggered in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.25999999999999,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "Though as I already mentioned here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 119.37899999999999,
          "en": "we don't wanna directly bind it to the submit event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.37899999999999,
          "end": 122.841,
          "en": "buttons that we want to call it indirectly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.841,
          "end": 127.699,
          "en": "So for that here in user input JS in the Submit Handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.699,
          "end": 131.25,
          "en": "we could expect that we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.25,
          "end": 135.758,
          "en": "a onCalculate prop on this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.758,
          "end": 138.69,
          "en": "And of course, since it's your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 141.6,
          "en": "this name is totally up to you, but I'm naming it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 145.539,
          "en": "onCalculate to make it clear that I want a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 145.539,
          "end": 149.46,
          "en": "as a value for this prop because in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.46,
          "end": 153.69,
          "en": "we wanna trigger this function when a certain event occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.69,
          "end": 156.537,
          "en": "in this case when the calculate button was clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.537,
          "end": 161.19,
          "en": "But then I call this function, which I received on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.19,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "the onCalculate prop and I'll pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 166.203,
          "en": "my user input state to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "So that's what we have to do in the user input component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "In the App.JS component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 178.92000000000002,
          "en": "we now have to set Calculate Handler, which does want a user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.92000000000002,
          "end": 183.303,
          "en": "input object as a value for this onCalculate prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.47,
          "end": 186.78,
          "en": "So in App.JS on this user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 189.873,
          "en": "we should now add the onCalculate prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.873,
          "end": 193.533,
          "en": "And if you chose a different name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.61,
          "end": 198.81,
          "en": "you also need to use a different name here as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 203.673,
          "en": "And then we set onCalculate equal to Calculate Handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 208.26,
          "en": "Now, calculateHandler already expects to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 212.588,
          "en": "get a user input object as it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.588,
          "end": 215.79,
          "en": "since I'm accessing a bunch of properties here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.79,
          "end": 218.574,
          "en": "and therefore of course we must make sure that an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.574,
          "end": 223.574,
          "en": "of that expected shape here is passed to onCalculate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 227.013,
          "en": "So to the calculate handler in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.45,
          "end": 230.995,
          "en": "Now if you are using different property names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 230.995,
          "end": 234.83100000000002,
          "en": "in your state here, different names than I am using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.83100000000002,
          "end": 238.8,
          "en": "you want to use those same names in this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 238.8,
          "end": 242.617,
          "en": "in the app component, in this Calculate handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 242.617,
          "end": 245.82,
          "en": "Because here I am trying to access the current",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 245.82,
          "end": 249.51,
          "en": "savings property and the yearly contribution property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 249.51,
          "end": 253.153,
          "en": "and so on, on that user input object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 253.153,
          "end": 256.35,
          "en": "So if you are using different property names here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 256.35,
          "end": 258.69,
          "en": "you have to use those different names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 258.69,
          "end": 260.853,
          "en": "in your CalculateHandler as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 261.9,
          "end": 266.9,
          "en": "With that though, we get all that data and I'm just going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.75,
          "end": 271.68,
          "en": "clean up those comments and we'll perform this calculation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 271.68,
          "end": 276.3,
          "en": "here with that input data to derive the yearly results",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 276.3,
          "end": 280.942,
          "en": "and now we need to do something with that yearly data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 280.942,
          "end": 284.043,
          "en": "So what is it that we want to do here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 284.90999999999997,
          "end": 289.32,
          "en": "Well, we can now store it as state because that would then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 289.32,
          "end": 294.033,
          "en": "allow us to pass that updated data to the Results Table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 294.897,
          "end": 299.897,
          "en": "So here in the app component, we can also call the use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 300.057,
          "end": 305.057,
          "en": "State Hook to store our yearly data and we could set it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 305.61,
          "end": 309.737,
          "en": "to null initially and then here get our results",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 310.573,
          "end": 315.033,
          "en": "and a set results function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 315.99,
          "end": 319.56,
          "en": "And now we could call set results here at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 319.56,
          "end": 324.03,
          "en": "of CalculateHandler to pass the yearly data, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 324.03,
          "end": 326.52,
          "en": "in the end is derived in this for loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 326.52,
          "end": 329.67,
          "en": "as a value to set results.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 329.67,
          "end": 332.403,
          "en": "Whoops, yearly data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 333.45,
          "end": 336.51,
          "en": "And with that it would be that yearly data that's managed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 336.51,
          "end": 338.373,
          "en": "as a state here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 339.69,
          "end": 344.49,
          "en": "Now I said could all the time because here we can now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 344.49,
          "end": 347.94,
          "en": "actually also deviate and change this code though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 347.94,
          "end": 350.15999999999997,
          "en": "if that's the solution you used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 350.15999999999997,
          "end": 353.15999999999997,
          "en": "it absolutely is fine, there's nothing wrong with it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 353.15999999999997,
          "end": 355.225,
          "en": "and you can stick to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 355.225,
          "end": 360.225,
          "en": "But here we could also switch to some derived state instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 360.963,
          "end": 365.961,
          "en": "And instead of storing the final results as state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 365.961,
          "end": 370.961,
          "en": "we could instead get our user input here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 372.579,
          "end": 377.579,
          "en": "and have a set user input state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 377.76,
          "end": 382.281,
          "en": "And in CalculateHandler, we can then call set user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 382.281,
          "end": 386.04,
          "en": "and pass the received user input object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 386.04,
          "end": 389.133,
          "en": "as a value to this state in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 390.18,
          "end": 393.51,
          "en": "And now we can grab all this data here where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 393.51,
          "end": 396.72,
          "en": "we create the yearly data and go through that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 396.72,
          "end": 401.459,
          "en": "for loop and cut it and delete this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 401.459,
          "end": 405.742,
          "en": "so that we have a very lean calculate handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 405.742,
          "end": 409.14,
          "en": "and instead add it here right inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 409.14,
          "end": 411.753,
          "en": "of the app component function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 414.36,
          "end": 418.74,
          "en": "With that, we would be rerunning this code whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 418.74,
          "end": 422.58,
          "en": "the state of this app component changes, and that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 422.58,
          "end": 426.66,
          "en": "of course means that whenever we receive new user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 426.66,
          "end": 429.45,
          "en": "so whenever we set this user input state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 429.45,
          "end": 431.94,
          "en": "this component function will re-execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 431.94,
          "end": 434.403,
          "en": "and this code will therefore re-execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 435.27,
          "end": 437.97,
          "en": "And with that, we would have the yearly data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 437.97,
          "end": 442.18,
          "en": "as derived state based on that user input state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 443.31,
          "end": 445.65,
          "en": "which is a slightly more elegant way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 445.65,
          "end": 449.19,
          "en": "of handling that though as mentioned, if instead you went",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 449.19,
          "end": 453.65999999999997,
          "en": "for the explicitly managed state, that would also be fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 453.65999999999997,
          "end": 456.69,
          "en": "but you should be aware of this alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 456.69,
          "end": 458.883,
          "en": "That's why I'm showing it to you here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 460.38,
          "end": 462.18,
          "en": "Now, one problem we'll have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 462.18,
          "end": 465.54,
          "en": "with this derived state approach here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 465.54,
          "end": 468.06,
          "en": "that I'm accessing all these properties here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 468.06,
          "end": 470.21,
          "en": "which potentially don't exist yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 470.21,
          "end": 473.46,
          "en": "if we have no user input yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 473.46,
          "end": 474.633,
          "en": "so if this is null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 475.83,
          "end": 480.232,
          "en": "Therefore we should actually wrap this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 480.232,
          "end": 485.232,
          "en": "with a if check where we check if user input is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 485.474,
          "end": 489.84,
          "en": "And if that's the case, we want to continue here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 489.84,
